**/fyers_session.json
**/fyers_login_state.txt
**/mt_accounts.json
**/*credentials*
**/*api_key*
# Found during the whole-project audit (2026-09-27). The FYERS webhook work
# wrote these next to kite_session.json, and .gitignore did not cover them: a
# live 53-byte webhook secret, the account snapshot, and the redacted-event
# log were each one `git add -A` away from history. Same rule as every other
# credential artifact on this list -- pulled with a credential, per-machine,
# regenerable from the API, never in git.
**/fyers_account.json
**/fyers_webhook_secret.txt
**/fyers_webhook_events.jsonl

# ── DATA — large, regenerable, or licensed ───────────────────────────────
# dataset/ (historical OHLCV) and the instrument masters are tracked since
# 2026-09-29 at the owner's request, so CI can run the `dataset` test tier.
# Everything pulled WITH a credential stays out: ticks, account, quotes,
# sessions, order intents (see below).
data/ticks/
data/fundamentals/
data/archive/
*.parquet
*.tick
*.duckdb

# ── Third-party reference clones — read for protocol facts, not vendored ─
research/reference/

# ── Research papers — licensed PDFs stay off the remote ──────────────────
research/papers/inbox/*.pdf
research/papers/processed/*.pdf
research/papers/rejected/*.pdf
research/replication/**/data/

# ── Models — large binaries, tracked in the registry not in git ──────────
models/artifacts/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.torchscript

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
*.binlog

# ── SEPARATE PROJECTS living in this folder — NOT part of Altair ────────
# Quants/ is QUANTLAB, its own research system (~3.5 GB). Nothing in Altair's
# build or docs references it. It belongs in its own repository; vacuuming it
# into Altair's history would be permanent and wrong.
Quants/

# ── Python virtualenvs ──────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: the `venv/` pattern below does NOT match `.venv/` — different names.
.venv/

# ── Predecessor Python tree — reference only, not part of the build ──────
RXT_trade/
RXT_trade 2/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/

# Exchange and broker master files are tracked with dataset/ (see DATA above).

# client/ devDependencies. TypeScript only, and it never ships.
node_modules/

# P2-12e: the Kite instrument master (8.8 MB) is tracked with dataset/.

# Account and quote snapshots hold live account state and market data
# pulled with a credential. Same rule as kite_session.json: they are
# regenerable from the API and must never enter git.
**/kite_account.json
**/kite_quotes.json
**/fyers_quotes.json
# P32-07. The live tick status file and any tick store the ticker writes.
# Same rule: pulled with a credential, and a tick store is a recording of a
# real session on a real account.
**/kite_ticks.json
# The FYERS live-feed status file and its optional JSONL recording: same rule.
**/fyers_ticks.json
**/fyers*.jsonl
# P33-01. The Live Forecast page fetches a recent window into this scratch
# directory on every click. Same rule as every other file on this list: it is
# market data pulled with a credential and regenerable from the API.
data/live_forecast_scratch/
# Data audit (ops/broker_audit.ps1, altair_data_audit): broker candles pulled
# with a credential, and the report / merged CSVs derived from dataset/. All
# regenerable; broker data is not ours to publish.
data/broker_audit/
data/verified/
# Pair-trading closes fetched from FYERS (ops/fetch_pairs.ps1): broker data,
# regenerable, not ours to publish.
data/pairs/
# NSE F&O bhavcopy files (ops/fetch_bhavcopy.ps1): bulky, fetched per machine.
data/bhavcopy/

# P36 hygiene. OPERATIONAL STATE, NOT SOURCE -- and git must not be able to
# DELIVER either of these.
#
# data/order_intents.jsonl is the queue oms/ drains. It was tracked, so an
# intent written by clicking around a dev machine's Terminal page could be
# committed, checked out somewhere else, and drained as though somebody had
# asked for it there. The UI cannot place an order by design (gate 3); a
# tracked queue would have routed around that with version control.
#
# data/kill_request.json is the same shape in the other direction: a committed
# halt request would trip a kill switch on whatever machine checked it out.
#
# Both are written by the running window, both are per-machine, and neither
# belongs in history.
data/order_intents.jsonl
data/kill_request.json
# The LIVE switch and the order router's book, journal and cursor: one
# machine's trading state, never shared.
data/live_trading.json
data/live_orders/
data/order_intents.jsonl.lock
**/*.altick

# GETSClient is a read-only reference UI/installer distribution (~1.8 GB) that
# lives in this folder. Quants/, RXT_trade/ and RXT_trade 2/ were already
# excluded; this one was not, so the whole tree sat stageable. It is not Altair
# source and must never enter the build or history.
GETSClient_5.0.191022_64bit_040924/

# Live terminal runtime state: universe, feed status, live-engine state and
# paper trades. Written at run time from broker data; never committed.
data/live/
